# STM32N6 CubeMX multi-context project. We track only hand-authored source +
# the .ioc (so the project is regenerable), and let CubeMX + stedgeai + the
# build reproduce everything else.
#
# Tracked: BallDetector_N6.ioc, scripts/, tests/, model/, README.md,
#          FSBL/Core/{Inc,Src} hand-authored files + main.c/it.c we edit,
#          FSBL/X-CUBE-AI/App/app_x-cube-ai.c (we add USER CODE hooks).
# Everything below is CubeMX/stedgeai/build output.

# --- generated build trees ---
Drivers/
Middlewares/
**/Debug/
**/Release/
build/
st_ai_ws/
.ai/

# --- X-CUBE-AI generated network code + weights (keep app_x-cube-ai.c) ---
# **/ so they match at the nested FSBL/X-CUBE-AI/App depth too.
**/X-CUBE-AI/App/network*.c
**/X-CUBE-AI/App/network*.h
**/X-CUBE-AI/App/network*generate_report.txt
**/X-CUBE-AI/App/*_info.json
**/X-CUBE-AI/App/constants_ai.h
**/X-CUBE-AI/App/*.onnx
**/X-CUBE-AI/App/LICENSE*.txt
*.raw

# my Phase-A manual stedgeai output at the top level — superseded by
# FSBL/X-CUBE-AI/ which CubeMX manages. Ignored so it can't get committed.
/X-CUBE-AI/

# --- ExtMemLoader is a generated helper context (flash-loader tool) ---
ExtMemLoader/

# --- CubeIDE workspace / build artifacts ---
.settings/
*.launch
*.elf
*.bin
*.map
*.list

# --- host-side test artifacts ---
tests/__pycache__/
scripts/__pycache__/
